  "schema:creditText": "\n**As a condition of use for this data, you MUST include this acknowledgement statement in publications as an attribution to the AMP RA/SLE funders and data contributors**\n1. Accelerating Medicines Partnership RA/SLE Network. AMP RA.SLE PhaseII CyTOF - version 5. Synapse https://doi.org/10.7303/SYN52623570.5 (2026).\n\n\"The results published here are in whole or in part based on data obtained from the ARK Portal (https://arkportal.synapse.org/). This work was supported by the Accelerating Medicines Partnership® Rheumatoid Arthritis and Systemic Lupus Erythematosus (AMP® RA/SLE) Program. AMP® is a public-private partnership (AbbVie Inc., Arthritis Foundation, Bristol-Myers Squibb Company, Foundation for the National Institutes of Health, GlaxoSmithKline, Janssen Research and Development, LLC, Lupus Foundation of America, Lupus Research Alliance, Merck & Co., Inc., National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases, National Institute of Arthritis and Musculoskeletal and Skin Diseases, Pfizer Inc., Rheumatology Research Foundation, Sanofi and Takeda Pharmaceuticals International, Inc.) created to develop new ways of identifying and validating promising biological targets for diagnostics and drug development Funding was provided through grants from the National Institutes of Health (UH2-AR067676, UH2-AR067677, UH2-AR067679, UH2-AR067681, UH2-AR067685, UH2- AR067688, UH2-AR067689, UH2-AR067690, UH2-AR067691, UH2-AR067694, and UM2- AR067678).\"",
  "schema:description": "AMP RA/SLE Phase II CyTOF of PBMC samples profiling marker panels targeting T cells, B cells, myeloid cells, and NK cells and total leukocyte (TL) samples profiling a marker panel targeting granulocytes.",
